WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.500
06:30 — Yard Today. At the yard Rashid opens Today on his phone across three business cars — what moves today, what waits.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:13.000
10:00 — Service iPad. iPad service board on the bench keeps the tiny fleet honest; gaps show up before a customer does.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:19.500
16:00 — Office laptop. Office laptop holds papers — registration, insurance — so “where is the file?” stops being a weekly sport.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:26.000
17:00 — Fuel costs. Fuel rollup on the laptop is illustrative; he uses it to see patterns, not to micromanage drivers by the litre.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:32.500
20:00 — Phone close. Phone confirms tomorrow’s plan. Three cars. Zero missing papers in his head.

